cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this study, please cite it as below."
title: "Do Kalshi prices match what happened? An actual-versus-expected study of prediction-market prices"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-12
authors:
  - family-names: Hong
    given-names: Harrison
license: MIT
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24177577
repository-code: "https://github.com/HarrisonHong21/kalshi-actual-vs-expected"
abstract: >-
  An actual-versus-expected study of 17,653 settled Kalshi NFL and NBA player-prop
  contracts from 88 games (5 October to 9 November 2026). Compares the price implied
  by each contract with how often it paid out, with game-cluster bootstrap intervals,
  a credibility standard, and a decomposition of a hypothetical buy-at-the-ask return
  into spread, fees and midpoint error. A study of prices; it contains no picks and
  is not betting advice.
keywords:
  - prediction markets
  - calibration
  - actual versus expected
  - bootstrap
  - Kalshi
